.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS12_PACK_P7ENCDATA 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS12_pack_p7encdata ,
.Nm PKCS12_pack_p7encdata_ex
.Nd Pack a set of PKCS#12 safeBags into a PKCS#7 encrypted data object
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs12.h
.Ft PKCS7 *
.Fo PKCS12_pack_p7encdata
.Fa "int pbe_nid"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "int passlen"
.Fa "unsigned char *salt"
.Fa "int saltlen"
.Fa "int iter"
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS12_SAFEBAG) *bags"
.Fc
.Ft PKCS7 *
.Fo PKCS12_pack_p7encdata_ex
.Fa "int pbe_nid"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "int passlen"
.Fa "unsigned char *salt"
.Fa "int saltlen"
.Fa "int iter"
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS12_SAFEBAG) *bags"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PKCS12_pack_p7encdata
generates a PKCS#7 ContentInfo object of encrypted-data type from the
set of safeBags
.Fa bags .
The algorithm ID in
.Fa pbe_nid
can be a PKCS#12 or PKCS#5 password based encryption algorithm, or a
cipher algorithm.
If a cipher algorithm is passed, the PKCS#5 PBES2 algorithm will be used
with this cipher as a parameter.
The password
.Fa pass
of length
.Fa passlen ,
salt
.Fa salt
of length
.Fa saltlen
and iteration count
.Fa iter
are inputs into the encryption operation.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_pack_p7encdata_ex
operates similar to the above but allows for a library context
.Fa ctx
and property query
.Fa propq
to be used to select the algorithm implementation.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
A
.Vt PKCS7
object if successful, or NULL if an error occurred.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
IETF RFC 2315
.Pf ( Lk https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2315 )
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr PKCS12_pbe_crypt_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn PKCS12_pack_p7encdata_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
